# Responsive = narrow fit **and** graceful growth

Canonical: `docs/DESIGN.md` § **Always responsive** · `docs/WEBSITES.md`.

## Law

Looking good on mobile is **not** enough. If Fit chips / short paired controls
fit on one line at the current content width, they **must** be one line.
Empty horizontal space beside a forever-`Down` toolbar on desk is a bug.

```text
❌ Hard-code flow: Down for Fit chip toolbars at every width
❌ Ship after phone-only screenshots
❌ Flatten every Down stack / force user-owned density “because wide”

✅ Stack / wrap only when measured width cannot hold the Fit children
✅ apply_responsive unlocks to Right once wide enough
✅ Check 320–390 **and** 1280 / 1920
✅ Exceptions exist (user density + other intentional layouts) — judge; if unsure leave alone
```

Law targets chrome / Fit toolbars. Exceptions are not exhaustive; most are
obvious — still take care.

Keep aligned with Kumkaj’s identical rule when either side tightens it.
